{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: under the I3 commission, write the first rules definition with named extents (source, infrastructure, rules) carrying per-extent review obligation, authority and effect class, composing across a mixed change, with the rules extent covering the rules definition, agent instruction files, CI and automation definitions and activations, met only with the rules scope's controller. Hugh's direction of 2026-10-05: a repository's layers must be distinguishable by customizable rules. Record any missing form as a delta with its owner; no lane digest changes; deliver within an I3 milestone with witnesses.","body":{"conditions":"(1) The first rules definition that I3 writes names extents instead of a flat first value: at least source, infrastructure and rules, each a declared class of resources with its own review obligation (who may meet it), its own authority (who may hold it), and its effect class (whether a landing in it is an effect with an outside destination and recovery). (2) Extents compose: a proposal touching several extents needs each extent's obligation met, and a reviewer outside an extent cannot meet it. (3) The rules extent covers the rules definition itself, agent instruction files (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and the like), CI and automation definitions, and the active-definition activations; its default controller is the rules scope's controller; a change there is never met by a feature reviewer alone. (4) Activation of a rules definition records what it checked, as the proof plan's O9 row asks; if the adopted texts lack a form this needs, record it as a delta with its owner and do not invent it in source. (5) This is scoped under the I3 commission bcf5ec17 and the proof plan's forthcoming acceptance story (the planner's request to the second planner filed alongside this one); it is filed as part of an I3 milestone with the usual witnesses, not as a separate source request. (6) No lane digest changes.","no_git_artifact":"true","prio